   \"S-reply-type\",\n        \"S-recovery\",\n        \"S-send\",\n        \"S-receive\",\n        \"S-formation\",\n        \"S-dispatch\",\n        \"S-init\"\n      ],\n      \"record\": {\n        \"path\": \"state.json\",\n        \"collection\": \"selections\",\n        \"match\": {\n          \"operation_id\": \"c529e73e2d674cd48c57212b1ab51e0c\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"feedback\": {\n        \"ref_ids\": [\n          \"S-reply-wire\",\n          \"S-reply-type\",\n          \"S-recovery\",\n          \"S-send\",\n          \"S-receive\",\n          \"S-formation\",\n          \"S-dispatch\",\n          \"S-init\"\n        ],\n        \"answered\": \"Initial source tracing connects A1 formation to A2 per-instance ballot authority: handlePropose allocates a local row instance; startPhase1 establishes command attributes and PreAccept state; replies are filtered by ballot and phase before fast commitment or Accept, and matching Accept replies can commit. Recovery creates new instance leadership bookkeeping, gathers a slow quorum of PrepareReply records, and selects command/attributes/status using VBallot. handlePrepare preserves the stored vbal while advancing bal and sends both. However PrepareReply.Marshal and Unmarshal encode/decode Ballot and Status but not VBallot. The actual transport invokes Marshal and allocates New objects before Unmarshal, so no transport-side reconstruction of this field is visible. This is source evidence of a representation discrepancy, not a validated consensus violation. Separately, startRecoveryForInstance overwrites inst.vbal with the attempted ballot before constructing its own reply; this local reply bypasses serialization and can compete with remote replies in highest-VBallot selection. The local and remote issues must be distinguished.\",\n        \"remaining\": [\n          \"Complete the initial backbone: quorum definitions and peer selection, commit propagation, execution dependencies, configuration, persistence/reconstruction and client completion boundaries remain to be traced before a usable map and formal Candidate.\",\n          \"Determine which legal histories produce relevant nonzero remote VBallot values and whether recovery selection changes after real serialization; preserve the distinct self-reply relabeling effect rather than attributing all recovery behavior to the codec.\",\n          \"handleAccept updates ballot and attributes without assigning ACCEPTED status in the inspected branch. Investigate whether another path supplies this status and what recovery is entitled to infer from a successful Accept reply.\",\n          \"Inspect initialization and resource lifecycle before constructing any execution witness. No formal execution or obligation has been submitted.\"\n        ],\n        \"understanding\": \"updated\",\n        \"rationale\": \"The producer, wire path and recovery consumer provide a concrete next discriminator without assuming that an arbitrary fabricated recovery state is reachable. Ballot/phase rejection and preservation of committed state are existing counterevidence that must remain in the eventual map and question.\",\n        \"question_updates\": {}\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"pending_work\": [],\n  \"current\": {\n    \"phase\": \"executed\",\n    \"operation_id\": \"c529e73e2d674cd48c57212b1ab51e0c\",\n    \"action\": \"research\"\n  },\n  \"latest_decision\": {\n    \"operation_id\": \"c529e73e2d674cd48c57212b1ab51e0c\",\n    \"action\": \"research\",\n    \"record\": {\n      \"path\": \"state.json\",\n      \"collection\": \"selections\",\n      \"match\": {\n        \"operation_id\": \"c529e73e2d674cd48c57212b1ab51e0c\"\n      }\n    }\n  },\n  \"stop\": {},\n  \"stop_reason\": \"Not started\",\n  \"explorations\": [],\n  \"review_issues\": [],\n  \"run_id\": \"469c7a22d6e54e44954d182578fd4bc1\",\n  \"snapshot_id\": \"46b4de4dbec54b2391f51afbc0243a6c\",\n  \"elapsed_seconds\": 203.252729111,\n  \"source_path\": \"/home/nitro/Desktop