{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"agent_message","text":"The formation and authority paths are now connected: replies advance an instance only within ballot and phase checks, while recovery gathers prior state and selects what to carry forward. Commit delivery and dependency execution add further guards. I’ll record that backbone and retain the codec, self-reply, and acceptance-status discrepancies as separate questions; none yet establishes a safety violation.\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > build_map.py <<'PY'\nimport json\nold=json.load(open('submission.json'))\nsources=old['sources']\nfor id,file,a,b in [('S-broadcast','epaxos/epaxos.go',435,612),('S-attributes','epaxos/epaxos.go',619,722),('S-commit','epaxos/epaxos.go',1066,1125),('S-execution','epaxos/exec.go',25,181),('S-base','replica/replica.go',63,177),('S-membership','master/master.go',120,235),('S-launch','run.go',23,102),('S-client','client/client.go',175,255),('S-application','state/state.go',75,155)]:\n sources.append(dict(id=id,file=file,start_line=a,end_line=b,kind='code_observation'))\ndef B(id,a,owner,ctx,trig,src,**kw):\n return dict(id=id,primary_activity=a,execution_owner=owner,protocol_context=ctx,trigger=trig,source_ids=src,**kw)\nb=[]\nb.append(B('B-formation','A1','EPaxos run goroutine, instance coordinator and recipient replicas','Replica/Instance row identity, initial ballot equals row owner','handlePropose -> startPhase1 -> handlePreAccept -> handlePreAcceptReply -> handleAccept/handleAcceptReply',['S-formation','S-attributes','S-broadcast','S-base'],implementation_guards=['PreAccept rejects ballot below inst.bal; ACCEPTED or later preserves attributes and only tries filling missing commands.','Reply handlers compare lastTriedBallot and phase. Fast commit requires FastQuorumSize()-1 replies plus initial ballot, equality and committed-dependency conditions; N<=3/thrifty skips equality, N>7 checks committed dependencies.','Slow commit counts acceptOKs+1>N/2. handleAccept rejects smaller ballots and avoids altering committed instances.'],writes=['Local proposal allocates crtInstance[Id], initializes PREACCEPTED commands/seq/deps and leader bookkeeping.','PreAccept recipient establishes PREACCEPTED or PREACCEPTED_EQ, bal/vbal and conflict indexes.','Accept recipient updates seq/deps/bal/vbal without assigning ACCEPTED; successful processing still replies with inst.bal.','Coordinator changes bookkeeping and local status to ACCEPTED or COMMITTED; commit calls updateCommitted.'],external_effects=['Thrifty broadcasts send PreAccept to FastQuorumSize()-1 live preferred peers and Accept to N/2. Commit goes to all live preferred peers.','When Dreply is false, coordinator replies on commit; default Dreply is true.'],async_boundaries=['Peer codec, per-type queue and select dispatch separate request/reply phases.'],produces_fact_ids=['F-state'],consumes_fact_ids=['F-state'],unknowns=['Does missing ACCEPTED assignment permit later preaccept/recovery to reinterpret support already acknowledged?','Quorum formulas and peer accounting require a separate responsibility check, especially configuration size boundaries.']))\nb.append(B('B-authority','A2','EPaxos per-instance recovery coordinator and prepare recipients','bal is joined ballot; vbal is stored value ballot; lb.lastTriedBallot is coordinator attempt','startRecoveryForInstance, makeBallot, handlePrepare and handlePrepareReply',['S-recovery','S-broadcast','S-commit'],implementation_guards=['Recovery returns for committed instances with commands.','Prepare raises bal for a larger request; returns current bal for lower requests.','Prepare reply requires preparing bookkeeping and exact lastTriedBallot. Quorum collection stops at SlowQuorumSize.'],writes=['Recovery replaces leader bookkeeping while preserving clientProposals, copies prior state then sets bal and vbal to attempted ballot before adding a self reply.','makeBallot uses local ID, adds N when recovering another row, and when IsLeader increments while below maxRecvBallot.','Recovery chooses fields from replies whose VBallot >= selected ballot; equal values use later iteration entries.','Committed selection installs state without broadcast; accepted or qualifying equal preaccept selection broadcasts Accept; other selection restarts phase one with recovered commands or NOOP.'],external_effects=['Prepare to live peers; handlePrepare sends prior value ballot/status/commands/attributes.','BeTheLeader only sets IsLeader true; it is not global exclusion of proposal owners.'],produces_fact_ids=['F-state','F-prepare'],consumes_fact_ids=['F-state','F-prepare'],cross_activity_effects={'A1':'Recovery selects the command/attributes/status used by subsequent Accept or PreAccept, so historical value context constrains new formation.'},unknowns=['Does the locally relabeled self reply overshadow eligible prior state?','makeBallot does not always strictly increase across retry; implications need legal histories.','TryPreAccept branch has duplicated selection predicate and may be unreachable from normal recovery.']))\nb.append(B('B-wire','A2','replica.SendMsg and replicaListener, then EPaxos run goroutine','PrepareReply for an acceptor and Replica/Instance under a requested ballot','replyPrepare -> SendMsg -> PrepareReply.Marshal; listener New/Unmarshal -> queue -> handlePrepareReply',['S-reply-type','S-reply-wire','S-send','S-receive','S-dispatch','S-broadcast'],reads=['PrepareReply.AcceptorId, Replica, Instance, Ballot, VBallot, Status, Command, Seq, Deps'],writes=['Codec writes/reads all listed fields except VBallot; New allocation leaves VBallot zero.'],external_effects=['Decoded object queued to registered RPC channel; no field reconstruction observed.'],async_boundaries=['TCP stream is read sequentially, but per-message goroutines delay then enqueue; handler order across messages is not guaranteed by receipt order.'],consumes_fact_ids=['F-prepare'],unknowns=['Which applicable field-preservation requirement and real producer history should a fixed codec check cover?']))\nb.append(B('B-recovery-trigger','A3','executeCommands goroutine and run goroutine','Known row prefixes and ExecedUpTo','Execution scan sees nil/noncommitted/commandless instance repeatedly',['S-dispatch','S-recovery'],writes=['Tracks problemInstance and timeout per row; sends recovery IDs for the blocked suffix when accumulated SLEEP_TIME_NS reaches COMMIT_GRACE_PERIOD.'],external_effects=['instancesToRecover dispatch calls startRecoveryForInstance.'],async_boundaries=['Scan retries after sleeping when no command executed; recovery is separate select work.'],cross_activity_effects={'A2':'Missing or incomplete instance state causes a fresh per-instance recovery attempt.','A1':'Recovered values return to decision formation.'},unknowns=['Progress under pending queues, repeated recovery and peer loss is not established by the nominal grace constant.']))\nb.append(B('B-config','A4','master registration, runReplica, base replica and EPaxos constructor','Fixed participant array from master; failures=(configured replica count-1)/2','registerWithMaster -> epaxos.New -> ConnectToPeers',['S-membership','S-launch','S-base','S-init','S-dispatch','S-broadcast'],writes=['Master assigns IDs by registered address and returns ready list at configured N. Replica sizes state and connections from nodeList.','EPaxos forces Thrifty=true; normal launch uses durable=false, batching=0, transconf=false; base Dreply=true.','Alive tracks peer connectivity; preferred order chooses recipients.'],cross_activity_effects={'A1':'FastQuorumSize=F+(F+1)/2; SlowQuorumSize=(N+1)/2; broadcast count and completion thresholds use these values or N/2.','A2':'IDs and N determine ballot construction.'},unknowns=['No dynamic membership path read; configuration mismatch and even-size applicability remain open.']))\nb.append(B('B-consume','A5','EPaxos run goroutine for commit; executeCommands and Exec for application','Per-instance committed state and dependency graph','handleCommit or local decision -> execution scan -> executeCommand/findSCC/strongconnect',['S-commit','S-execution','S-dispatch','S-formation','S-application'],implementation_guards=['handleCommit ignores already committed/executed state and smaller ballots.','Execution requires COMMITTED, commands present, and traversed dependencies committed or executed with commands.'],writes=['Commit installs commands, seq/deps and bal/vbal; updates conflict index and committed prefix.','SCC members ordered by seq, row, then proposeTime; execution marks EXECUTED.'],external_effects=['Default Dreply executes commands and replies for instances retaining client proposals; otherwise PUT executes without reply.','NOOP commit for own row may requeue outstanding client proposals.'],produces_fact_ids=['F-state'],consumes_fact_ids=['F-state'],cross_activity_effects={'A1':'Only committed dependencies are consumed for application ordering.','A7':'Replies after execution carry command ID and result for retained proposals.'},unknowns=['Same-row/sequence tie ordering and range-command conflict tracking remain unexamined responsibilities.']))\nb.append(B('B-persistence','A6','EPaxos metadata/command writers','Durable option; normal launcher disables it','recordInstanceMetadata, recordCommands, sync',['S-init','S-launch','S-base'],writes=['When enabled, metadata writes bal then vbal to the same four bytes, followed by status/seq/deps; commands serialized separately.'],durable_effects=['Guarded StableStore.Write and Sync calls; base StableStore initialized nil.'],cross_activity_effects={'A2':'Would preserve ballot history only if configured and reconstructed; no reconstruction was found in inspected EPaxos/base source.'},unknowns=['Durable startup and crash-restart contract are not established; do not infer supported recovery from writers alone.']))\nb.append(B('B-client','A7','Client send functions and replica proposal admission','Client command IDs and selected destination','SendWrite/SendRead/SendScan -> SendProposal; GetReplyFrom',['S-client','S-formation','S-execution','S-launch'],writes=['Client increments seqnum for commands; sends to leader or closest peer unless Fast fanout enabled.','handlePropose batches channel entries; TODO explicitly leaves retry handling unresolved.'],external_effects=['Returns command ID at send; GetReplyFrom decodes reply separately.'],cross_activity_effects={'A1':'Admitted commands form instance batches.','A5':'Default completion is emitted during dependency execution.'},unknowns=['Retry/deduplication and concurrent invocation contract require further caller investigation.']))\nf=[dict(id='F-state',meaning='Replica-local stored command/attributes/status with joined ballot bal and value ballot vbal for an instance; status reports local phase and does not itself prove a quorum.',identity={'replica':'row ID','instance':'row-local instance number','holder':'local replica'},validity_context='Live InstanceSpace entry; phase and ballot changes can replace or reinterpret it. No restart persistence guarantee assumed.',representation=['Instance.Cmds, Seq, Deps, Status, bal, vbal'],invalidators=[],reinterpreters=['B-authority','B-formation','B-consume'],durability='Normal launch is volatile; optional writer is not a demonstrated restore mechanism.',recovery='Prepare reports stored state; recovery selects replies then may restart phase one, Accept, or install committed state.',source_ids=['S-formation','S-recovery','S-commit','S-init'],unknowns=['Eligibility of acknowledged Accept state when Status remains preaccepted.']),dict(id='F-prepare',meaning='A handlePrepare-produced reply reports the acceptor current joined ballot and stored value ballot, status, commands and attributes for the requested instance.',identity={'acceptor':'PrepareReply.AcceptorId','replica':'PrepareReply.Replica','instance':'PrepareReply.Instance'},validity_context='Snapshot constructed after processing Prepare; direct self-reply construction in startRecoveryForInstance instead reports locally modified bal/vbal. Wire representation is not assumed faithful.',representation=['PrepareReply fields, including separate Ballot and VBallot'],invalidators=[],reinterpreters=['B-wire','B-authority'],durability='Transient message; no persistence.',recovery='Consumed in the preparing attempt after Ballot comparison; VBallot drives prior-state selection.',source_ids=['S-recovery','S-reply-type','S-reply-wire'],unknowns=['Effect of wire omission versus independent self-reply relabeling in reachable recovery histories.'])]\nroles=json.load(open('../research.json'))['activity_roles']\nactivities=[]\nfor a,r in roles.items():\n bs=[x for x in b if x['primary_activity']==a]\n activities.append(dict(class_id=a,applicability='applicable',purpose=r['relation'],realization_summary=' '.join(x['trigger'] for x in bs),entry_points=[x['id'] for x in bs],source_ids=list(dict.fromkeys(s for x in bs for s in x['source_ids'])),unknowns=[]))\ndef path(ex,ids,fs,src): return dict(explanation=ex,behavior_ids=ids,fact_ids=fs,source_ids=src)\nover=dict(status='usable',rationale='Representative formation, per-instance authority, prior-support transfer, delivery and execution have been traced. Concrete anomalies remain questions, not assumed guarantees.',formation=path('Client admission allocates an owner-row instance, computes dependencies and sequence from conflicts and preaccepts. Live preferred peers establish or retain local state and reply. Coordinator filters reply ballot/phase, merges attributes, and commits on fast-path predicates or sends Accept. Matching Accept replies plus self support can commit. Commit broadcasts full commands/attributes; receivers reject stale ballots or already-decided state. Execution waits for committed command-bearing dependency graph components before application and default client completion.',['B-formation','B-config','B-consume','B-client'],['F-state'],['S-formation','S-broadcast','S-base','S-commit','S-execution']),context=path('Authority is per-instance: original row ballot equals owner ID. Recipients reject below joined bal; Prepare advances bal and reports vbal/history. Incomplete execution prefixes trigger recovery. Recovery replaces bookkeeping, obtains matching-ballot replies, and selects prior state by VBallot before choosing Accept, phase-one restart, or committed installation. A leader flag chan